+++ b/docs/eval_harness_design.md
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
+- `generateReport({ evaluations, thresholds })` takes an optional `thresholds` object such as `{ exact_match: 0.9 }`. When given, the report gains `passed` and a `thresholds` list of `{ metric, min, score, passed }`; a metric with no score, or absent from `evaluations`, fails. Without `thresholds` the report shape is unchanged. The CLI `--threshold` option uses the same logic.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
